# ============================================
# REQUIRED SERVER-SIDE RESPONSE HEADERS
# ============================================
# The following headers MUST be added by the dev team to ALL inference endpoints
# (NMT, ASR, TTS, etc.) to enable automated non-inference timing analysis

# 1. X-Trace-Id (CRITICAL - Required for Jaeger integration)
#    Purpose: Returns the actual OpenTelemetry trace_id (NOT correlation_id)
#    Format: 32-character hexadecimal string
#    Example: X-Trace-Id: b73aed39bcb99b002efd12136465ef95
#
#    Implementation (Python):
#      from opentelemetry import trace
#      span = trace.get_current_span()
#      response.headers["X-Trace-Id"] = format(span.get_span_context().trace_id, '032x')

# 2. X-Inference-Model-Time (CRITICAL - Required for non-inference metrics)
#    Purpose: Time spent ONLY in ML/GPU inference (Triton server calls)
#    Format: Milliseconds (will be converted to seconds in load test)
#    Example: X-Inference-Model-Time: 105.3
#
#    Implementation (Python):
#      inference_start = time.time()
#      result = await triton_client.infer(...)
#      inference_time = time.time() - inference_start
#      response.headers["X-Inference-Model-Time"] = f"{inference_time:.3f}"

# 3. X-Non-Inference-Time (OPTIONAL - Nice to have)
#    Purpose: Time spent in API overhead (auth, DB, preprocessing, postprocessing)
#    Format: Seconds with 3 decimal places
#    Example: X-Non-Inference-Time: 4.139
#    Calculation: total_time - inference_time

# EXISTING HEADERS (already implemented):
#    x-correlation-id: Internal correlation ID (different from trace_id)
#    x-process-time: Total processing time in seconds

# HOW TO CALCULATE NON-INFERENCE TIME:
# non_inference_time = x-process-time - (X-Inference-Model-Time / 1000)
# Example: 1.953s (total) - (105.3ms / 1000 = 0.105s ML) = 1.848s (API overhead)
#
# WHY THIS IS NEEDED:
# - x-correlation-id != trace_id (they are different values)
# - Without X-Trace-Id, we cannot query Jaeger API for trace details
# - Without X-Inference-Model-Time, we cannot separate ML time from API overhead
# - Currently load tests can only measure total time, not the breakdown
